Bloody Phone 📱🩸

George was a 17-year-old boy who worked to earn money. He wanted to buy a new phone, so he decided to order one online.

While browsing, he found a phone that was advertised as very cheap and extremely fast.

George thought, “Even if I get scammed, it’s fine. I just want a phone quickly.”

So he placed the order.

Surprisingly, the phone arrived only 10 hours later.

George opened the package and tested it. The phone was actually incredibly fast.

He paid the delivery person. George was about to say thank you, but the delivery person left without waiting.

George simply thought, “It’s okay. I already paid him.”

George used the phone for one week.

However, he noticed something strange. The phone's background showed pictures of children.

George ignored it.

After another two weeks, the phone suddenly began displaying bloody scenes.

George was confused.

“Why is this happening?”

He took the phone to a repair shop.

But when the repairman checked it, the bloody scenes had completely disappeared. The phone was behaving normally.

The repairman looked at George and said:

«“Brother, I don't see any problem with your phone.”»

George took the phone back.

When he looked at it again, the phone had returned to the normal background he had set.

George continued using it for another four weeks.

Then everything changed.

The phone became broken. The screen no longer worked normally.

And on the screen was a moving, extremely terrifying face.

George immediately smashed the phone.

Suddenly, the face inside the broken phone emerged as a humanoid creature.

The creature stood there and began counting.

“One…”

“Two…”

“Three…”

“Four…”

“Five.”

George was still standing there.

The humanoid looked at him.

Then, moving incredibly fast, it attacked George and consumed him completely.

Afterward, it threw what remained of George back into the phone.

Then the humanoid itself entered the phone.

The phone returned to its original normal state.

But now, among the pictures of the children, there was a new picture.

George's picture.

After this tragic incident, the phone was taken far away and thrown into a volcano.

The volcano completely destroyed the phone.

The phone—and the humanoid inside it—were finally destroyed.

The End.
